WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.672
(audience cheer and applaud)

00:00:01.672 --> 00:00:02.594
- [Kelly] Okay, I had my-

00:00:02.594 --> 00:00:03.450
- Wow!

00:00:03.450 --> 00:00:05.940
- I had my teeth made 'cause
I couldn't sing with them,

00:00:05.940 --> 00:00:07.213
so here we go, okay okay.

00:00:07.213 --> 00:00:08.400
- Is this Invisalign?

00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:09.233
What's happening?

00:00:09.233 --> 00:00:10.329
- I literally, it is like
a little, but I was like,

00:00:10.329 --> 00:00:13.650
I can't sing a song like this.

00:00:13.650 --> 00:00:14.590
- [Kyle] No, you're fully
committed right now.

00:00:14.590 --> 00:00:16.080
- Yeah, I'm committed.

00:00:16.080 --> 00:00:17.580
I don't know if I'll have to take them out

00:00:17.580 --> 00:00:18.413
for this interview

00:00:18.413 --> 00:00:20.608
because I'm eating the teeth
right now, but it's fine.

00:00:20.608 --> 00:00:22.446
- (lisping) Do you want
me to talk like this too

00:00:22.446 --> 00:00:23.507
so it's even and fair?

00:00:23.507 --> 00:00:25.220
- Yeah, just make me
feel good about myself.

00:00:25.220 --> 00:00:27.810
Do you love Halloween? Do you
dress up? Do you get into it?

00:00:27.810 --> 00:00:29.166
- I love Halloween.

00:00:29.166 --> 00:00:29.999
- [Kelly] Me too.

00:00:29.999 --> 00:00:31.020
- I have a real connection with Halloween.

00:00:31.020 --> 00:00:32.319
- [Kelly] Oh yeah.

00:00:32.319 --> 00:00:33.450
- You know, my co-star
when I was a little girl,

00:00:33.450 --> 00:00:35.468
when I was five years old, Michael Landon,

00:00:35.468 --> 00:00:37.052
his birthday was Halloween.

00:00:37.052 --> 00:00:38.204
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:00:38.204 --> 00:00:39.037
- And I always loved him so much.

00:00:39.037 --> 00:00:41.300
And then I did some
horror films, you know,

00:00:41.300 --> 00:00:43.320
- [Kelly] A few, yeah.

00:00:43.320 --> 00:00:45.900
- Yes, and then also my daughter,

00:00:45.900 --> 00:00:48.510
my eldest daughter Farrah
is born on Halloween.

00:00:48.510 --> 00:00:49.950
- I didn't know that, that's cool.

00:00:49.950 --> 00:00:52.244
- Yeah, so we love to like decorate.

00:00:52.244 --> 00:00:54.480
As soon as Halloween, October hits,

00:00:54.480 --> 00:00:56.367
my whole house is
decorated, inside and out,

00:00:56.367 --> 00:00:59.100
because to me it's like the
kick off of all the holidays.

00:00:59.100 --> 00:00:59.933
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:00:59.933 --> 00:01:01.050
- [Kyle] And it's like
Thanksgiving, Christmas.

00:01:01.050 --> 00:01:03.150
- [Kelly] That is true,
it's the kickoff, yeah.

00:01:03.150 --> 00:01:05.010
Oh, I love the decorations.

00:01:05.010 --> 00:01:06.090
- [Kyle] Thank you.

00:01:06.090 --> 00:01:07.860
That's my dining table at home right now.

00:01:07.860 --> 00:01:09.406
- Okay, so I do wanna come back to you,

00:01:09.406 --> 00:01:11.945
Farrah, who was born on Halloween.

00:01:11.945 --> 00:01:14.670
You went, so you're like having Halloween,

00:01:14.670 --> 00:01:16.470
like carving pumpkins
and you go into labor?

00:01:16.470 --> 00:01:17.777
- Yes, I was 19 years old,

00:01:17.777 --> 00:01:20.340
I was carving a pumpkin and I was pregnant

00:01:20.340 --> 00:01:21.750
and went into labor.

00:01:21.750 --> 00:01:24.570
and she was born at 8:13 on Halloween.

00:01:24.570 --> 00:01:25.710
- I mean, it's kind of incredible

00:01:25.710 --> 00:01:27.372
'cause your family's
probably all together anyway.

00:01:27.372 --> 00:01:29.700
- Oh, my family, we have all,

00:01:29.700 --> 00:01:31.798
my sisters, Kathy, Kim and I,

00:01:31.798 --> 00:01:32.631
we've all, when we've given birth,

00:01:32.631 --> 00:01:35.430
we've all been in the hospital
rooms with each other.

00:01:35.430 --> 00:01:36.263
- Oh wow.

00:01:36.263 --> 00:01:39.150
- And her husband Rick
videotaped all our births.

00:01:39.150 --> 00:01:40.889
I know that sounds
really weird, but he did.

00:01:40.889 --> 00:01:42.094
(audience laugh)

00:01:42.094 --> 00:01:43.560
And yeah, so when I looked up,

00:01:43.560 --> 00:01:45.030
I had my sisters for moral support,

00:01:45.030 --> 00:01:46.254
I was a young Mom, I was terrified.

00:01:46.254 --> 00:01:47.910
- Yeah.

00:01:47.910 --> 00:01:49.927
- And I had friends there,

00:01:49.927 --> 00:01:52.440
my Mom was at the Polo
Lounge in Beverly Hills

00:01:52.440 --> 00:01:55.110
and brought like half
the polo lounge with her.

00:01:55.110 --> 00:01:57.390
And I looked up and at one
point there was 19 people

00:01:57.390 --> 00:01:58.701
in the room when I gave birth.

00:01:58.701 --> 00:02:00.156
- That's a little...

00:02:00.156 --> 00:02:02.190
- It's a little much.

00:02:02.190 --> 00:02:03.023
- It's a little much,

00:02:03.023 --> 00:02:04.133
I mean, for you, I just mean
that would be overwhelming.

00:02:04.133 --> 00:02:06.436
- My sister Kathy took the baby first

00:02:06.436 --> 00:02:09.150
and then she looked at my then husband

00:02:09.150 --> 00:02:10.620
and said, would you like to hold the baby?

00:02:10.620 --> 00:02:12.270
So generous, you know?

00:02:12.270 --> 00:02:13.380
- Oh my God, no,

00:02:13.380 --> 00:02:15.060
so here's the thing
about, did you do this?

00:02:15.060 --> 00:02:16.350
Like, I was so terrified.

00:02:16.350 --> 00:02:17.700
I don't know why, but I was so terrified,

00:02:17.700 --> 00:02:19.290
especially with my first kid,

00:02:19.290 --> 00:02:21.150
that somebody was gonna take my baby.

00:02:21.150 --> 00:02:24.270
So I looked at my sister,
like grabbed her and my ex

00:02:24.270 --> 00:02:26.455
and I was like, if you
lose sight of my daughter,

00:02:26.455 --> 00:02:28.620
I will never love you again.

00:02:28.620 --> 00:02:29.580
- I had that same thing.

00:02:29.580 --> 00:02:31.830
- I need you to follow wherever she goes.

00:02:31.830 --> 00:02:33.976
And like, I was like so nervous about it.

00:02:33.976 --> 00:02:34.809
- Because you hear those stories.

00:02:34.809 --> 00:02:36.030
- [Kelly] I know!
- I also have that fear.

00:02:36.030 --> 00:02:36.863
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:02:36.863 --> 00:02:37.846
Yes.

00:02:37.846 --> 00:02:38.880
- It's a little irrational,
but I don't care.

00:02:38.880 --> 00:02:41.100
So, wait, so do you believe
in like, supernatural stuff?

00:02:41.100 --> 00:02:43.410
Have you ever seen ghosts
or, I haven't and I want to.

00:02:43.410 --> 00:02:45.363
- Oh, come over to my house.

00:02:46.560 --> 00:02:48.040
Yes, I have.
- I don't know if

00:02:48.040 --> 00:02:49.230
they'd show themselves to me,

00:02:49.230 --> 00:02:50.850
- Thank God they haven't
actually shown themselves

00:02:50.850 --> 00:02:52.440
'cause I don't know, I
wouldn't be here right now.

00:02:52.440 --> 00:02:53.939
- I would want to see it.

00:02:53.939 --> 00:02:54.772
(audience laugh)

00:02:54.772 --> 00:02:55.887
- You think that, you think that?

00:02:55.887 --> 00:02:58.140
- No, I 100% think it would be cool.

00:02:58.140 --> 00:03:00.210
- Okay, well I've had some things happen.

00:03:00.210 --> 00:03:02.923
I've lost both my parents and
I've had some things happen.

00:03:02.923 --> 00:03:03.859
- Okay.

00:03:03.859 --> 00:03:05.103
- Like a lot of things happen,

00:03:05.103 --> 00:03:06.163
especially after my mom passed away,

00:03:06.163 --> 00:03:10.770
or very strange things
happen, like lights going on

00:03:10.770 --> 00:03:12.450
where they weren't even plugged in,

00:03:12.450 --> 00:03:13.320
really weird things.

00:03:13.320 --> 00:03:14.550
- Yeah.

00:03:14.550 --> 00:03:16.110
- So I have no doubt I believe in that.

00:03:16.110 --> 00:03:18.960
And then my house that I live
in now was built in like 1882

00:03:18.960 --> 00:03:21.341
and moved by like trolley in 1912.

00:03:21.341 --> 00:03:22.174
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:03:22.174 --> 00:03:23.910
- And I hear footsteps a lot,

00:03:23.910 --> 00:03:25.620
everyone in my family
has heard the footsteps.

00:03:25.620 --> 00:03:26.453
- Yeah.

00:03:26.453 --> 00:03:30.180
- And Smokey Robinson
actually used to own my home,

00:03:30.180 --> 00:03:32.333
and I was at an Oscar
party this past Oscars.

00:03:32.333 --> 00:03:33.166
- [Kelly] Oh.

00:03:33.166 --> 00:03:35.310
- And he said, oh, have you
heard the footsteps yet?

00:03:35.310 --> 00:03:36.627
I did not need to hear that.

00:03:36.627 --> 00:03:37.542
(audience laugh)

00:03:37.542 --> 00:03:38.513
(Kelly gasps)

00:03:38.513 --> 00:03:40.560
- I was like, I wanted to
believe that I was imagining it,

00:03:40.560 --> 00:03:43.110
but the funny thing is
that it feels safe though.

00:03:43.110 --> 00:03:44.280
It's like a good experience.

00:03:44.280 --> 00:03:46.233
- Yeah, I don't feel
unsafe around it, yeah.

00:03:46.233 --> 00:03:48.501
- Yeah but we've seen the movies,

00:03:48.501 --> 00:03:49.408
we don't know what's gonna happen.

00:03:49.408 --> 00:03:50.430
- Those are movies though.

00:03:50.430 --> 00:03:51.383
I really wanna see one Kyle, okay.

00:03:51.383 --> 00:03:52.878
(audience applaud)

00:03:52.878 --> 00:03:54.120
Looks like a not a fun dinner party.

00:03:54.120 --> 00:03:56.070
It seemed like it didn't go well.

00:03:56.070 --> 00:03:58.650
- So I don't have a lot of luck

00:03:58.650 --> 00:04:00.030
with dinner parties apparently.

00:04:00.030 --> 00:04:00.863
- [Kelly] Okay.

00:04:00.863 --> 00:04:02.880
- So yeah, we had a dinner
party season one called,

00:04:02.880 --> 00:04:05.040
we referred to it as the
dinner party from Hell.

00:04:05.040 --> 00:04:05.873
- Yeah.

00:04:05.873 --> 00:04:09.258
- This is supposedly on
par, if not worse than that.

00:04:09.258 --> 00:04:10.518
- [Kelly] Oh no.

00:04:10.518 --> 00:04:13.053
- Yeah, that was actually a crazy night,

00:04:13.053 --> 00:04:15.780
everybody lost their marbles.

00:04:15.780 --> 00:04:18.660
And we had like, current
housewives and past housewives.

00:04:18.660 --> 00:04:20.070
We had Camille Grammar there.

00:04:20.070 --> 00:04:21.600
Denise Richards, Faye Resnick was there,

00:04:21.600 --> 00:04:22.620
we had the entire cast

00:04:22.620 --> 00:04:26.700
and it just had the makings
of just a complete disaster.

00:04:26.700 --> 00:04:28.537
- You know, the producers were like, yeah.

00:04:28.537 --> 00:04:32.700
- Yeah, I mean I of
course, there was tears,

00:04:32.700 --> 00:04:33.960
there was screaming and you know,

00:04:33.960 --> 00:04:36.064
of course they're like, are you okay?

00:04:36.064 --> 00:04:37.650
Oh and you'll be fine, right?

00:04:37.650 --> 00:04:39.358
I'm like, yeah, they do love that.

00:04:39.358 --> 00:04:40.629
- I have to say though,

00:04:40.629 --> 00:04:41.490
I've gone through public
separation and divorce.

00:04:41.490 --> 00:04:42.750
That is the worst thing ever.

00:04:42.750 --> 00:04:44.280
We were talking about in commercial break,

00:04:44.280 --> 00:04:47.190
how do you, I feel like I
was on TV the whole time too,

00:04:47.190 --> 00:04:48.480
but in a different way.

00:04:48.480 --> 00:04:49.770
Like, y'all shoot reality

00:04:49.770 --> 00:04:52.546
so they got everything
kind of behind the scenes.

00:04:52.546 --> 00:04:53.610
- They did.

00:04:53.610 --> 00:04:55.410
And it was like, you
know, it's really hard

00:04:55.410 --> 00:04:58.200
because, we're going through,

00:04:58.200 --> 00:05:01.407
we are separated, it's amicable,

00:05:01.407 --> 00:05:04.410
but it's still really difficult.

00:05:04.410 --> 00:05:07.980
And I wasn't quite ready
to share in the beginning.

00:05:07.980 --> 00:05:09.900
And it was, it's just
painful no matter what.

00:05:09.900 --> 00:05:11.335
- Yeah.

00:05:11.335 --> 00:05:12.570
- This is not what my
fairytale was supposed to be.

00:05:12.570 --> 00:05:13.403
- [Kelly] Girl.

00:05:13.403 --> 00:05:14.520
- So it is really hard.

00:05:14.520 --> 00:05:15.510
And everybody's weighing in

00:05:15.510 --> 00:05:17.430
and people all of a sudden
like, you crushed our dreams.

00:05:17.430 --> 00:05:19.441
You know, we don't believe in true love.

00:05:19.441 --> 00:05:20.358
I'm like, no, we really.

00:05:20.358 --> 00:05:21.599
We had an amazing love story
- You're like, what do you

00:05:21.599 --> 00:05:22.602
think I think about true love
- [Kyle] for a very long time.

00:05:22.602 --> 00:05:23.435
- right now?

00:05:23.435 --> 00:05:24.335
- [Kyle] Yeah, exactly!

00:05:24.335 --> 00:05:25.228
- Like where do you think
I'm at on the spectrum.

00:05:25.228 --> 00:05:26.061
- I'm gonna worry about my family,

00:05:26.061 --> 00:05:27.300
now I've gotta worry about
a few million people too,

00:05:27.300 --> 00:05:28.133
what what they think.
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:05:28.133 --> 00:05:29.760
- And it makes it a lot more difficult.

00:05:29.760 --> 00:05:31.035
- Yeah.

00:05:31.035 --> 00:05:32.970
I do think though, being able to be

00:05:32.970 --> 00:05:34.290
that vulnerable in that situation

00:05:34.290 --> 00:05:35.580
is probably gonna help a lot of people

00:05:35.580 --> 00:05:38.970
just relate to it and
feel not alone in it.

00:05:38.970 --> 00:05:39.930
'cause that's the worst.

00:05:39.930 --> 00:05:42.660
That grief and loss, even
if it's something you want,

00:05:42.660 --> 00:05:44.400
it's something that went terribly wrong

00:05:44.400 --> 00:05:45.652
that you did not see coming, you know?

00:05:45.652 --> 00:05:46.590
- [Kyle] Yeah.

00:05:46.590 --> 00:05:47.778
- And that's hard.

00:05:47.778 --> 00:05:49.233
- And everybody wants to put

00:05:49.233 --> 00:05:50.513
their spin on what they think it is.

00:05:50.513 --> 00:05:52.800
- Yeah, when they really,
usually don't know it all.

00:05:52.800 --> 00:05:54.180
- And they know so much about your life.

00:05:54.180 --> 00:05:55.300
- Yeah.

00:05:55.300 --> 00:05:56.285
- And they think that we deserve to know

00:05:56.285 --> 00:05:57.335
everything that's going on,

00:05:57.335 --> 00:05:58.168
like, what caused this, what happened?

00:05:58.168 --> 00:05:59.010
And then if you don't tell them,

00:05:59.010 --> 00:06:00.450
they come up with their own idea.

00:06:00.450 --> 00:06:01.980
So it's just, you know.

00:06:01.980 --> 00:06:03.402
- Which is super fun.

00:06:03.402 --> 00:06:04.290
(she laughs)

00:06:04.290 --> 00:06:05.123
- It's so much fun, it's so much fun.

00:06:05.123 --> 00:06:06.360
I love reading lies about myself everyday.

00:06:06.360 --> 00:06:07.193
- Yeah, it is so fun.

00:06:07.193 --> 00:06:09.162
And my Mom calls me and my Mom,

00:06:09.162 --> 00:06:11.591
I'm like, people lie,

00:06:11.591 --> 00:06:13.569
I'm like, Mom, it's a lie.

00:06:13.569 --> 00:06:15.450
It's not like real, like, what's in there,

00:06:15.450 --> 00:06:16.703
and she's like,

00:06:16.703 --> 00:06:17.536
I don't know well people
are gonna believe this.

00:06:17.536 --> 00:06:18.660
And I'm like, just let it go, Elsa.

00:06:18.660 --> 00:06:19.974
- It's so hard, I know!

00:06:19.974 --> 00:06:23.100
- But you, I have to ask this too.

00:06:23.100 --> 00:06:25.830
So y'all, you went to a psychic,
y'all did a psychic reading

00:06:25.830 --> 00:06:29.100
and people are saying that
they predicted this separation.

00:06:29.100 --> 00:06:30.362
- Well yes, season one.

00:06:30.362 --> 00:06:34.140
She said that your husband does
not emotionally fulfill you.

00:06:34.140 --> 00:06:34.991
She said to me.

00:06:34.991 --> 00:06:37.830
But funniest thing is
that now everyone's like,

00:06:37.830 --> 00:06:39.186
oh, she was right, she predicted this.

00:06:39.186 --> 00:06:41.217
But she also said, oh,
it's your second marriage,

00:06:41.217 --> 00:06:42.630
oh, then you're fine,

00:06:42.630 --> 00:06:43.463
you won't get divorced.

00:06:43.463 --> 00:06:46.020
I really do feel like
she was picking up on

00:06:46.020 --> 00:06:48.390
Camille Grammar because
she was hiding their issues

00:06:48.390 --> 00:06:51.360
and Kelsey did end up leaving, you know,

00:06:51.360 --> 00:06:53.130
and they were going
through their thing so,

00:06:53.130 --> 00:06:54.897
I stand by that because
we really were very happy

00:06:54.897 --> 00:06:56.890
for a very long time, very long time.

00:06:56.890 --> 00:06:57.990
- Yeah, very long time, years.

00:06:57.990 --> 00:07:00.120
- I still consider us a success story, so.

00:07:00.120 --> 00:07:00.953
- Yeah.

00:07:00.953 --> 00:07:01.786
You know, what's so funny.

00:07:01.786 --> 00:07:03.930
So after all of it, I say
that to him, I'm like,

00:07:03.930 --> 00:07:05.250
you know, I'm not gonna
poo poo on the whole thing.

00:07:05.250 --> 00:07:06.960
Like, there were really great parts

00:07:06.960 --> 00:07:08.448
and even if it was one
sided in certain areas,

00:07:08.448 --> 00:07:10.140
like it still was real for me.

00:07:10.140 --> 00:07:11.040
And it was beautiful for me.

00:07:11.040 --> 00:07:12.120
And I think that's wonderful,

00:07:12.120 --> 00:07:14.010
'cause not everybody feels in life,

00:07:14.010 --> 00:07:15.167
not everybody gets a chance.

00:07:15.167 --> 00:07:16.535
(audience cheer and applaud)

00:07:16.535 --> 00:07:17.368
And I think that's beautiful
to be able to feel that.

00:07:17.368 --> 00:07:19.665
And you know it exists, you know?

00:07:19.665 --> 00:07:22.470
Okay, so do you ever have plans to retire?

00:07:22.470 --> 00:07:23.820
'Cause 13 years,

00:07:23.820 --> 00:07:25.920
I feel like I'm looking at like
Blake Shelton on the Voice.

00:07:25.920 --> 00:07:27.540
Like, it's like, you know what I'm saying?

00:07:27.540 --> 00:07:28.373
Like that's hard.

00:07:28.373 --> 00:07:29.206
I was looking at him, I was like,

00:07:29.206 --> 00:07:30.039
this is gonna be hard for you man.

00:07:30.039 --> 00:07:31.636
This is like a life for you.

00:07:31.636 --> 00:07:32.469
- I'm thinking about
what Portia said to me

00:07:32.469 --> 00:07:33.302
when she was little right now.

00:07:33.302 --> 00:07:34.967
- Yeah, you're not dead, you can't quit.

00:07:34.967 --> 00:07:38.548
- You know, I don't see myself
ever quitting, you know,

00:07:38.548 --> 00:07:40.860
acting and things like that.

00:07:40.860 --> 00:07:44.290
That's my first love, but of
course there's times I think,

00:07:44.290 --> 00:07:47.188
this has to come to an end at some point.

00:07:47.188 --> 00:07:51.091
It's not necessarily, aligned
with who I am at times,

00:07:51.091 --> 00:07:54.960
because it can be very
difficult and challenging

00:07:54.960 --> 00:07:56.334
and provokes me my anxiety.

00:07:56.334 --> 00:07:57.180
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:07:57.180 --> 00:07:59.837
- But it's hard because
it's really woven into,

00:07:59.837 --> 00:08:02.575
my life for so many years.

00:08:02.575 --> 00:08:05.490
It would be very painful
even to walk away from

00:08:05.490 --> 00:08:08.100
just the crew and production and all that,

00:08:08.100 --> 00:08:09.840
because I love those people so much.

00:08:09.840 --> 00:08:10.980
- Yeah, I do understand that.

00:08:10.980 --> 00:08:12.090
I think people don't realize that

00:08:12.090 --> 00:08:12.930
when they're watching at home,

00:08:12.930 --> 00:08:14.040
how invested you get with people.

00:08:14.040 --> 00:08:15.120
- People become your family.

00:08:15.120 --> 00:08:16.276
- Yeah.

00:08:16.276 --> 00:08:17.191
- It's very hard.

00:08:17.191 --> 00:08:18.024
- You see them more than your family.

00:08:18.024 --> 00:08:18.857
- Exactly.

00:08:18.857 --> 00:08:20.460
So one day it'll come though.

00:08:20.460 --> 00:08:21.293
That day will come.

00:08:21.293 --> 00:08:23.280
- Alright, alright, well
we need another break.

00:08:23.280 --> 00:08:25.320
But you can see the Real
Housewives of Beverly Hills

00:08:25.320 --> 00:08:28.220
Wednesdays on Bravo and streaming
the next day on Peacock.

